        </grid><grid id="283"><property name="marginTop">8pt</property><property name="width">10.1in</property><column id="284"/><row id="285"><cell id="286"><property name="backgroundColor">#edf5ff</property><property name="borderLeftColor">#0043ce</property><property name="borderLeftStyle">solid</property><property name="borderLeftWidth">3px</property><property name="paddingTop">6pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">6pt</property><property name="paddingLeft">10pt</property><property name="paddingRight">10pt</property><label id="287"><property name="fontSize">8.5pt</property><property name="fontWeight">bold</property><property name="color">#161616</property><text-property name="text">Reading the mix</text-property></label><label id="288"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="color">#525252</property><property name="marginTop">2pt</property><text-property name="text">A maintenance organisation that controls its work spends most hours on preventive and predictive work and on planned corrective work found by it, and few on emergencies. A month where the red band grows is a month where the plan was overtaken by breakdowns.</text-property></label></cell></row></grid><grid id="292"><property name="pageBreakBefore">always</property><property name="pageBreakInside">avoid</property><property name="marginTop">18pt</property><property name="width">10.1in</property><column id="293"/><row id="294"><cell id="295"><label id="289"><property name="fontSize">7.5pt</property><property name="color">#0f62fe</property><property name="fontWeight">bold</property><property name="letterSpacing">0.32pt</property><text-property name="text">2  ·  EQUIPMENT RELIABILITY</text-property></label><label id="290"><property name="fontSize">14pt</property><property name="color">#161616</property><property name="marginTop">2pt</property><property name="marginBottom">2pt</property><text-property name="text">Bad actors: the assets that fail most</text-property></label><label id="291"><property name="fontSize">8.5pt</property><property name="color">#525252</property><property name="marginBottom">8pt</property><text-property name="text">Corrective and emergency work orders on assets completed in the period (failures). MTBF is the period divided by the asset's failures; MTTR is the average actual start-to-finish time of its repairs (repairs over 30 days are left out).</text-property></label></cell></row></grid>
        <table id="348">
            <property name="width">10.10in</property>
            <property name="dataSet">dsBadActors</property>
            <list-property name="boundDataColumns">
