        </table><data id="656"><list-property name="visibility"><structure><property name="format">all</property><expression name="valueExpr" type="javascript"><![CDATA[rows_dsStores > 0]]></expression></structure></list-property><property name="fontSize">8.5pt</property><property name="color">#6f6f6f</property><property name="paddingTop">10pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">10pt</property><property name="paddingLeft">8pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><list-property name="boundDataColumns"><structure><property name="name">v</property><expression name="expression" type="javascript"><![CDATA[smrpEmpty("dsStores", "No storerooms.")]]></expression><property name="dataType">string</property></structure></list-property><property name="resultSetColumn">v</property></data><grid id="661"><property name="pageBreakBefore">always</property><property name="pageBreakInside">avoid</property><property name="marginTop">18pt</property><property name="width">10.1in</property><column id="662"/><row id="663"><cell id="664"><label id="659"><property name="fontSize">7.5pt</property><property name="color">#0f62fe</property><property name="fontWeight">bold</property><property name="letterSpacing">0.32pt</property><text-property name="text">APPENDIX</text-property></label><label id="660"><property name="fontSize">14pt</property><property name="color">#161616</property><property name="marginTop">2pt</property><property name="marginBottom">2pt</property><text-property name="text">Method and definitions</text-property></label></cell></row></grid><grid id="725"><property name="width">10.1in</property>
            <column id="726"><property name="width">1.7in</property></column><column id="727"><property name="width">8.4in</property></column><row id="665"><cell id="666"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="667"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="fontWeight">bold</property><property name="color">#161616</property><text-property name="text">Period</text-property></label></cell>
                <cell id="668"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="669"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="color">#525252</property><text-property name="text">By default the 12 complete months before the run date. If the database has no regular work order activity in that window (a test or archive copy), the period ends at the last month with regular activity, and the header says so. Set End_Month (YYYY-MM) and Months to choose the period yourself; Site limits the report to one site.</text-property></label></cell></row><row id="670"><cell id="671"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="672"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="fontWeight">bold</property><property name="color">#161616</property><text-property name="text">Work categories</text-property></label></cell>
                <cell id="673"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="674"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="color">#525252</property><text-property name="text">Preventive: work types in Preventive_Types (default PM, PMCAL, CAL) and any work order generated by a PM. Predictive / condition-based: Predictive_Types (default PDM, CBM). Corrective: Corrective_Types (default CM, CMCAL). Emergency: Emergency_Types (default EM, EMCAL), the reactive part of corrective work. Everything else (capital, projects, events) is Other. Set the parameters to your own work types.</text-property></label></cell></row><row id="675"><cell id="676"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="677"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="fontWeight">bold</property><property name="color">#161616</property><text-property name="text">Completed work</text-property></label></cell>
                <cell id="678"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="679"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="color">#525252</property><text-property name="text">Work orders of class WORKORDER (tasks included for hours and cost) in a completed or closed status, by actual finish date. Status checks go through the status synonyms, so renamed statuses count correctly.</text-property></label></cell></row><row id="680"><cell id="681"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="682"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="fontWeight">bold</property><property name="color">#161616</property><text-property name="text">Failures</text-property></label></cell>
                <cell id="683"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="684"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="color">#525252</property><text-property name="text">Corrective and emergency work orders on an asset. Rework is a failure that started within 30 days of the previous failure on the same asset being completed. Downtime comes from asset status changes (ASSETSTATUS); downtime reported against preventive work is scheduled, the rest unscheduled.</text-property></label></cell></row><row id="685"><cell id="686"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="687"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="fontWeight">bold</property><property name="color">#161616</property><text-property name="text">Compliance</text-property></label></cell>
                <cell id="688"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="689"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="color">#525252</property><text-property name="text">PM &amp; PdM compliance: preventive work orders due in the period (PM due date, else target finish, else scheduled finish) completed by the end of the due day. Schedule compliance: work orders with a scheduled finish in the period completed by the end of that day. Maximo keeps no frozen weekly schedule, so this is the closest measure.</text-property></label></cell></row><row id="690"><cell id="691"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="692"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="fontWeight">bold</property><property name="color">#161616</property><text-property name="text">Planned work</text-property></label></cell>
                <cell id="693"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="694"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="color">#525252</property><text-property name="text">Hours on work orders that had a labour estimate or a job plan before they were done.</text-property></label></cell></row><row id="695"><cell id="696"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="697"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="fontWeight">bold</property><property name="color">#161616</property><text-property name="text">Stores</text-property></label></cell>
                <cell id="698"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="699"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="color">#525252</property><text-property name="text">Inventory value is the current balance at average cost (standard or last cost when no average). Stock-outs are reorder-managed items with no balance, a stand-in for SMRP's unfilled-request measure. Records accuracy uses physical counts and count adjustments in the period.</text-property></label></cell></row><row id="700"><cell id="701"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="702"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="fontWeight">bold</property><property name="color">#161616</property><text-property name="text">Reference values</text-property></label></cell>
                <cell id="703"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="704"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="color">#525252</property><text-property name="text">The common reference column holds industry rules of thumb often quoted with the SMRP metrics. SMRP itself publishes definitions and formulas, not targets for your plant: agree targets locally and watch the trend.</text-property></label></cell></row><row id="705"><cell id="706"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="707"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="fontWeight">bold</property><property name="color">#161616</property><text-property name="text">Not in Maximo</text-property></label></cell>
                <cell id="708"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="709"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="color">#525252</property><text-property name="text">Overall equipment effectiveness and other production-loss and unit-of-output metrics need production data from the plant systems. They are listed so the pack covers every SMRP pillar.</text-property></label></cell></row><row id="710"><cell id="711"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="712"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="fontWeight">bold</property><property name="color">#161616</property><text-property name="text">What is read</text-property></label></cell>
                <cell id="713"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="714"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="color">#525252</property><text-property name="text">WORKORDER, ASSET, ASSETSTATUS, LABOR, LABTRANS, INVENTORY, INVBALANCES, INVCOST, MATUSETRANS, INVTRANS, SYNONYMDOMAIN, MAXVARS. Every query is a SELECT; nothing is created or changed. Runs with the Maximo database login on SQL Server, Oracle and Db2.</text-property></label></cell></row><row id="715"><cell id="716"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="717"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="fontWeight">bold</property><property name="color">#161616</property><text-property name="text">SMRP</text-property></label></cell>
                <cell id="718"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="719"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="color">#525252</property><text-property name="text">Metric names and formulas follow the SMRP Best Practices metrics (Society for Maintenance &amp; Reliability Professionals). Metric numbering differs between editions, so the report uses the metric names.</text-property></label></cell></row><row id="720"><cell id="721"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="722"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="fontWeight">bold</property><property name="color">#161616</property><text-property name="text">Author</text-property></label></cell>
                <cell id="723"><property name="paddingTop">3pt</property><property name="paddingBottom">3pt</property><property name="borderBottomColor">#e0e0e0</property><property name="borderBottomStyle">solid</property><property name="borderBottomWidth">1px</property><label id="724"><property name="fontSize">8pt</property><property name="color">#525252</property><text-property name="text">Created by Mohamed Chihaoui.</text-property></label></cell></row></grid>
    </body>
</report>
